<%# locals: (title:, meta: nil, meta_title: nil, label: nil, tabs: [], tabs_data: {}, actions_html: nil, data: {}, row_class: "-mx-4 px-4") %>
<%# THE PAGE HEADER: the second layer of the triple stack (docs/PAGE_HEADER.md).
    navbar, then this row, then a table's sticky header, each below the last.

    AT REST it has no background and no border: a title on the left, tabs on the
    right. ONCE STUCK under the navbar it takes the bar. Its box never changes
    between the two, so a state change moves nothing and republishes nothing.

      title         the page's one h1.
      meta          short text beside the title, such as the version. Hidden on a
                    phone, where the tabs need the width.
      meta_title    the meta's title attribute.
      label         the nav's accessible name. A row with tabs needs it.
      tabs          [{ label:, href:, current:, data: }]. `current` is the
                    aria-current value ("page" or "true"), and blank on the others.
      tabs_data     data attributes for the tabs' scroller.
      actions_html  a control on the right, for a row with no tabs.
      data          data attributes for the row, such as the page's own controller.
      row_class     the bleed. The default fits a container with px-4; pass "" in a
                    container with no gutter of its own.

    THE ROW IS NEVER A <header>. studio/pinned_stack takes the document's first
    <header> as the navbar, so on a page with no navbar this row would publish as
    --nav-bottom.

    IT JOINS THE STACK WITH data-pin="page" AND POSITIONS OFF --pin-page-top, the
    bottom of everything above it. --pin-stack-bottom includes the row's own edge,
    so a row positioned off it would chase itself down the page. Anything below,
    such as the sticky table header's clone, sits under the row with no edit.

    THE SENTINEL stays at the row's place in the flow, and the row's distance from
    it is what "stuck" means, on every kind of header. It is absolutely positioned,
    so a space-y parent adds nothing for it. It carries the controller, so the row
    keeps its data-studio-controller for the page's own. So the row carries no top
    margin: the space above it belongs to its container. %>
<div class="page-header-sentinel" data-studio-controller="page-header" aria-hidden="true"></div>
<%= content_tag(tabs.any? ? :nav : :div,
      class: "page-header sticky #{row_class}".strip,
      style: "top: var(--pin-page-top, var(--nav-bottom, var(--nav-h, 0px))); z-index: var(--z-sticky, 30)",
      aria: { label: label.presence },
      data: data.merge(pin: "page")) do %>
  <div class="page-header-lead">
    <h1 class="page-header-title"><%= title %></h1>
    <% if meta.present? %>
      <p class="page-header-meta label-upper"<%= %( title="#{ERB::Util.h(meta_title)}").html_safe if meta_title.present? %>><%= meta %></p>
    <% end %>
  </div>
  <% if tabs.any? %>
    <%= tag.div(class: "page-header-tabs", data: tabs_data) do %>
      <div class="page-header-track">
        <% tabs.each do |tab| %>
          <%= link_to tab.fetch(:label), tab.fetch(:href),
                class: "btn btn-sm #{tab[:current].present? ? 'btn-primary' : 'btn-neutral'}",
                aria: { current: tab[:current].presence },
                data: tab.fetch(:data, {}) %>
        <% end %>
      </div>
    <% end %>
  <% elsif actions_html.present? %>
    <div class="page-header-actions"><%= actions_html %></div>
  <% end %>
<% end %>
